From 74f243ab74c2a8fe07ea4d68b9f870d051707e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:12:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the context ring draws the 5-hour quota window as
 an outer arc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.26 (ask 46). The ring's tooltip already listed
every quota window the agent reported, but the ring itself drew only
the context: the 5-hour limit, the one that runs out within a working
session, took a hover to see. The ring now carries it as a thin outer
arc, info-coloured, warning-coloured when the agent flags the window.

It is drawn only when a five_hour window has arrived. Plans differ in
which windows their usage report fills -- on this machine's the
report carries seven_day alone -- and Claude Agent (Plus) already
forwards only the windows the report fills (toQuotaWindow drops a
null or absent one). So the window's presence is the rule, not the
plan's name: the SDK names plans pro/max/team/enterprise, and a rule
on a name breaks the day a plan is renamed. A window that came without
a utilization has nothing to draw and gets no arc, as the tooltip
shows it as a dash.

Without the window the ring is returned untouched, at its 16 px, so
nothing moves for a plan that has none. With it, the two arcs share a
20 px box: the context ring keeps its radius (ring_size / 2 -
stroke_width, as CircularProgress derives it) and the outer arc sits
2 px outside it. Only the single-ring branch gains it; the split
input/output rings are the native agent's, which reports no quota.

AccountUsage gains window(kind), a lookup the arc reads.

Tests: thread_view::tests::five_hour_arc_tests (no window, no arc; a
reported window draws its fill and its flag; an unmeasured window
draws nothing and an off-scale one is clamped);
acp_thread tests::account_usage_finds_a_window_by_kind. Seen failing
with five_hour_arc and window() returning None.
---

diff --git a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
index 348897b..0a1f9f6 100644
--- a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
+++ b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
@@ -3887,6 +3887,12 @@ impl AccountUsage {
         self.windows.is_empty()
     }
 
+    /// One window by kind, if the agent has reported it. The context ring draws the 5-hour
+    /// window as an outer arc only when this returns it (Zeo next §6.26).
+    pub fn window(&self, kind: &AccountUsageWindowKind) -> Option<&AccountUsageWindow> {
+        self.windows.get(kind)
+    }
+
     /// The window closest to its limit, which is the one worth surfacing when there is
     /// room for only one.
     pub fn most_constrained(&self) -> Option<&AccountUsageWindow> {
@@ -9948,6 +9954,19 @@ mod tests {
         assert_eq!(window.utilization, Some(0.85));
     }
 
+    #[test]
+    fn account_usage_finds_a_window_by_kind() {
+        let mut usage = AccountUsage::default();
+        usage.ingest(&rate_limit("seven_day", "allowed", 0.4));
+        assert!(
+            usage.window(&AccountUsageWindowKind::FiveHour).is_none(),
+            "a plan whose report has no 5-hour window has none to draw"
+        );
+        usage.ingest(&rate_limit("five_hour", "allowed", 0.25));
+        let window = usage.window(&AccountUsageWindowKind::FiveHour).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(window.utilization, Some(0.25));
+    }
+
     #[test]
     fn account_usage_reports_no_change_when_nothing_moved() {
         let mut usage = AccountUsage::default();
diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs
index b4784c0..d9aea93 100644
--- a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs
+++ b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs
@@ -6832,14 +6832,19 @@ impl ThreadView {
                     .mt_px()
                     .mr_1()
